 Interview Questions
 Q1. Why Validation?

 To ensure only valid data enters the application and reaches the business logic.

 Q2. Why validate in DTO instead of Service?

 DTO is the first point where request data enters the application. Invalid requests are rejected early before business logic executes.

 Q3. Difference between @NotNull and @NotBlank?

 @NotNull

 Checks only for null.

 @NotBlank

 Checks for null, empty string, and whitespace.
 Used for Strings.
 Q4. What does @Valid do?

 It triggers Bean Validation on the request object before the controller method executes.

 Q5. What happens if validation fails?

 Spring throws a MethodArgumentNotValidException, which is usually handled by a Global Exception Handler to return a 400 Bad Request.

